# Code owners.
#
# @bendaamerahmed is a placeholder — see OPEN-DECISIONS.md #2. `npm run
# check:release-gate` fails while it is unresolved, so a release cannot ship
# with review authority pointing at nobody.
#
# The point of this file is not blanket ownership. It is that four categories of
# change can silently weaken the agent's safety properties, and each needs a
# reviewer who knows why the property exists.

# Default.
*                                   @bendaamerahmed

# The agent definition. Its frontmatter carries four load-bearing decisions
# (background:false, no AskUserQuestion, no isolation, no maxTurns), each with an
# ADR and a Tier 0 rule. See CONTRIBUTING.md "Changing the safety properties".
/plugins/backstage-idp/agents/      @bendaamerahmed

# Skill content is what the agent acts on. A wrong assertion here is worse than
# no skill, because the agent will act on it confidently.
/plugins/backstage-idp/skills/      @bendaamerahmed

# The rules themselves. A weakened rule is invisible in a content diff.
/test/tier0/                        @bendaamerahmed
/test/tier1/                        @bendaamerahmed

# Every version-sensitive fact the plugin asserts, and the staleness budget that
# decides when the currency job starts failing.
/baseline.json                      @bendaamerahmed

# Workflow changes can disable a required check without touching a test.
/.github/workflows/                 @bendaamerahmed

# The trust model an adopting security review reads.
/SECURITY.md                        @bendaamerahmed
